{#- Hard vs soft installation: copy from the current primeturf.co.za homepage. -#}
<section class="section section--tint" id="installation" aria-labelledby="install-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Installation</p>
      <h2 id="install-title" class="display-l" data-reveal>What’s the difference between a soft and a hard installation?</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="install">
      <article class="install__card" data-reveal>
        <p class="label install__kind">Hard installation</p>
        <h3 class="install__title">On paving, concrete, tiles or pool surrounds</h3>
        <p>A hard installation involves professionally bonding artificial turf directly onto an existing hard surface such as paving, concrete, tiles or pool surrounds.</p>
        <p>Since the base is already in place, minimal preparation is required. We thoroughly clean and prepare the surface before applying premium adhesives to ensure a neat, secure and long-lasting finish.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="install__card" data-reveal>
        <p class="label install__kind">Soft installation</p>
        <h3 class="install__title">On natural ground or soil</h3>
        <p>A soft installation is used where artificial turf is installed on natural ground or soil. It follows our professional 7-step installation process, which creates a durable foundation for years of enjoyment.</p>
        <ol class="steps7">
          <li>Weed prevention</li>
          <li>Precision levelling</li>
          <li>Proper drainage</li>
          <li>A structurally stable base</li>
          <li>Professional compaction</li>
          <li>Secure bonding</li>
          <li>Precision installation</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="fine">The result is a natural-looking, realistic lawn with exceptional durability.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
